  "change": {
    "near_end_after_restore": "a turn whose prefix is restored from a snapshot inside the cache lookup now saves its next checkpoint one token before its prompt end, captured inside the same prefill pass. Before, such a turn saved the last 128-aligned position instead; when that position fell in the first 128 tokens of the appended text, the prefill ran as two passes (+150-175 ms; appends of 129-383 tokens, under 1 % of real requests). Same capture plan as the restore path that already used it.",
    "redundant_prompt_image": "each long turn of a conversation with images kept three nearly equal snapshots (one token before the prompt end, the prompt end with its logits, the completed turn). The rule that protects the two longest snapshots kept the last two, and the first one, which is the one a follow-up that re-renders the previous answer restores, was evicted when another conversation filled the sixteen slots. A prompt-end snapshot whose near-end snapshot is cached now yields first; an exact retry of the same prompt restores the near-end one plus one short pass instead."
  },
